 "class_note": "The confusion classes are built from Azure's IPA phoneme symbols, and only en-US returns them named. The counts below come from the five en-US reads and are the first real phoneme evidence in this file — the en-GB single pass of 09-14 to 09-16 returned every symbol EMPTY, so the spelling-based fallback (classify_word) was carrying the classes alone and undercounting badly: i/ii 15 -> 50, s/z 8 -> 44, schwa 7 -> 32, b/v 9 -> 24. The 09-14 read still contributes spelling guesses only (see locale_note). phonemes_before_2026_09_16 holds the old two-pass tallies from before the regression.",
 "locale_note": "SCORING LOCALE IS en-US SINCE 2026-09-16, at the user's decision. Microsoft's docs make en-US the only locale that returns prosody AND named IPA phonemes. Five of the six reads were re-assessed under it on the SAME audio, the SAME stored Whisper transcript and the SAME span reference — only the locale changed. Prosody moved from 52-59 to 81-86, fluency up about 3 points, accuracy and completeness within a point or two either way, and the SHAPE of the series held (09-12 still the weak read). So the locale changed the levels, not the trend. THE 09-14 READ IS STILL en-GB: at 84 minutes it is the longest, and a single request that long is refused outright (CancellationReason.Error 1007, 'Quota exceeded' — NOT the month; see quota_note). Its prosody of 59.4 and pron of 80.6 are en-GB numbers and DO NOT belong on the same line as the rest; its accuracy, fluency and completeness are close enough to read with care. It stays stranded until long reads are CHUNKED, which is unbuilt. Re-run only after that: .venv-practice/bin/python scripts/rescore-reads.py --only 2026-09-14",
 "quota_note": "CORRECTED 2026-09-20. This file and CLAUDE.md said the Azure F0 month was spent and scoring was blocked. It was not. A live probe (scripts/azure-check.py) returns Success with IPA phonemes and prosody 91.3 on the same key. What actually fails is ONE REQUEST THAT IS TOO LONG: the 83.7-minute read is refused with CancellationReason.Error 1007 'Quota exceeded', while the 9.5, 15.3, 24.2, 27.6 and 37.1-minute reads all rescored normally. The ceiling on a single continuous-recognition request sits somewhere above ~37 minutes, and Azure words it exactly like an exhausted monthly allowance, which is what misled the diagnosis for four days. Probe with a short utterance before ever blaming the month again — it costs seconds.",
